PRETABLE block -- lunaabsentcpu (#503) pass-2 repair, probe v3 (sessions A, A2, B, B2, C, C2, D, E), written BEFORE table 2 runs.
2026-09-06 ~10:10.  Corrections, if any, go to a SEPARATE file (PRETABLE2_lunaabs.correction.out) so this file's mtime stays the order proof.
DIFF UNDER THE TABLE: (1) the fix's capture site moves BELOW the DEVINIT `ncpus > 4' exit (Fable pass 1, minimax pass 2: the bound is
  <= MAX_CPUS by construction, not by that exit); (2) three new sessions: B2 `sio5 deliver' (a DEVICE line delivering to the connected
  slot 0 -- deepseek; grok's ask-again M_SWONLY), C2 `both deliver' (both slots pending on -n 2 -- kimi), E `four cpus' / `cpu3 deliver' /
  `others idle' (-n 4, the LAST slot -- glm, grok); (3) docstring corrections (stale 20/20 predictions -> measured; the sio5clr channel
  note; the contract's catches/does-not-catch lists).
SIBLING PARITY: slot 0 now has a device-line delivery row beside its software-interrupt one (B vs B2); slots 1 and 3 have delivery rows
  (C, E); slot 2 is walked at -n 4 and pinned only by `others idle' (it must NOT enter).  A delivery row for slot 2 is not owed by any
  enumerated mutant: M_AND1 aliases slot 3 onto slot 1, so its kill is cpu 3 NOT entering (`cpu3 deliver' STOP) and possibly cpu 1
  entering instead (`others idle' BADREGS); slot 2 aliased onto slot 0 has nothing pending in E and asserts nothing.
CLAIM -> ROW: every new contract sentence names its row (above).
GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD: the walk's body reads interrupt_status (now varied by device line, B2), interrupt_enable[cpu], software_interrupt_
  status[cpu] (now two slots at once, C2), irqActive[cpu] (per-slot, C2), cpu_irq[cpu] (slots 0..3, E).  The disagreeing states each new
  mutant builds are named per row below.
CHANNEL per new row (mutant -> observable):
  sio5 deliver   M_MASK30 (`status = interrupt_status & ~(1 << 30)')  cpu 0 never enters (STOP after 15 s) vs pc == VBR+8
  sio5 deliver   M_SWONLY (`if (!software_interrupt_status[cpu]) continue;')  same channel; the software rows B/C/E stay green
  both deliver   M_IRQACTIVE0 (all four `irqActive[cpu]' -> `irqActive[0]')  only one cpu enters (STOP naming the set) vs both enter
  cpu3 deliver   M_AND1 (`cpu_irq[cpu & 1]' both calls)  cpu 3 never enters (STOP) -- and cpu 1 may enter instead (others idle BADREGS)
  cpu3 deliver   M_MIN2 (`ncpus = min(ncpus, 2)')  slot 3 never walked -> cpu 3 never enters (STOP)
  the eleven v2 mutants are re-run on v3 for the record: their kills should be unchanged (M_NULLAB and M_NOREASSERT stay green).
